sequenceDiagram
  actor Organizer
  actor Participant
  participant CLI as make local / make down
  participant Host as Managed Bun process
  participant DB as SQLite and original keys
  participant Docker as Owned Docker projects
  Organizer->>CLI: make local
  CLI->>Host: Acquire controller ownership and start
  Host->>DB: Recover retained events and authentication
  Note over Host,Docker: New on-demand jobs remain stopped until participant resume
  Host-->>Organizer: Organizer and participant URLs
  Organizer->>Host: Create teams, prepare dormant jobs, start event
  Participant->>Host: Start / resume
  Host->>Host: Check team/global/memory admission limits
  Host->>Docker: Create or resume owned project
  Participant->>Host: Stop (keep data)
  Host->>Docker: Stop; retain writable layer and volumes, not RAM
  Organizer->>CLI: make down
  CLI->>Host: Authenticate ownership-bound shutdown
  Host->>Docker: Stop remaining owned running containers; retain data
  Host->>DB: Drain and retain competition state
  Host-->>CLI: Shutdown result
  Note over Organizer,Docker: No automatic eviction or reset; AWS stacks remain; event clock is not reset
  Note over Host,Docker: Existing events retain their legacy lifecycle
